{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 1: The AND Gate",
  "description": "Learn how a single neuron can compute logical AND.\n\nChallenge: Adjust the weights in the Linear layer to make this network \noutput ON only when BOTH inputs are high (1.0).\n\nHint: AND gate needs positive weights and a negative bias around -1.5.\nThink about it: with weights of 1.0 each, the sum is 0, 1, or 2.\nWhere should the threshold be to only activate when sum = 2?",
