    {
      "id": "comment-tutorial-1",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Tutorial: The AND Gate",
      "position": [
        1628,
        105
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": " THE AND GATE - Your First Neural Network!\n\nWhat even IS a neural network? It's a math machine that\nlearns to make decisions. This tiny one has just ONE\nneuron - the purple 'Linear' box. Let's see how it works!\n\nFOLLOW THE FLOW (left to right):\n1. INPUT A and INPUT B: Your two switches (0=off, 1=on)\n2. CONCAT: Bundles both inputs together into [A, B]\n3. LINEAR (the neuron): Does the actual thinking!\n4. SIGMOID: Squishes the result between 0 and 1\n5. OUTPUT: Shows ON if result > 0.5, OFF otherwise\n\nHOW THE NEURON THINKS:\nIt multiplies each input by a 'weight' (how important\nthat input is), adds them up, then adds a 'bias'\n(a nudge to shift the decision point).\n\n  result = (A * weight1) + (B * weight2) + bias\n  result = (A * 1.0) + (B * 1.0) + (-1.5)\n\nSo with weights=1 and bias=-1.5:\n  Both OFF (0,0): 0 + 0 - 1.5 = -1.5  (very negative = OFF)\n  One ON  (1,0): 1 + 0 - 1.5 = -0.5  (still negative = OFF)\n  One ON  (0,1): 0 + 1 - 1.5 = -0.5  (still negative = OFF)\n  Both ON (1,1): 1 + 1 - 1.5 = +0.5  (positive = ON!)\n\nThat's AND logic! Only +0.5 is positive, so only\nboth-inputs-on produces ON. The bias of -1.5 sets the\nbar high enough that you need BOTH inputs to clear it.\n\nTRY IT: Toggle the sliders and watch the output change!",
        "width": 420,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Floating explanatory text"
    },
